NAME
       nano - a small, easy text editor

SYNOPSIS
       nano [FILE]

DESCRIPTION
       nano is a simple editor for the terminal. Unlike vi there are no
       modes: what you type goes into the file. The commands are Ctrl key
       combinations, and the most important ones are listed at the bottom of
       the screen, where ^ means Ctrl and M- means Alt.

KEYS
       Ctrl+O  save the file (write Out); Enter confirms the name
       Ctrl+X  leave (asks whether to save changes)
       Ctrl+W  search (Where is)
       Ctrl+K  cut the current line
       Ctrl+U  paste the cut text
       Ctrl+G  help
       Ctrl+C  show the cursor position

EXAMPLES
           nano /etc/hosts
           EDITOR=nano crontab -e

SEE ALSO
       vim(1), vi(1)
